§ `C. Article 1(2): when a Law is passed (V1 only)`

-- C02  V1 src:6: confirmed in Council 2020-06-01 and registered 2020-06-10: not deemed passed until both, so on 2020-06-10, the later
#ASSERT `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2020 6 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 6 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 6 10
-- C04  V1 src:6: registered 2020-06-05 and confirmed 2020-06-10: the later is 2020-06-10
#ASSERT `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2020 6 15) (YMD 2020 6 10) (YMD 2020 6 5) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 6 10
-- C02b  both on the same day
#ASSERT `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2020 6 15) (YMD 2020 6 10) (YMD 2020 6 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 6 10
-- C07  V1 src:6 "unless a contrary intention appears"
#ASSERT REFUSED `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2020 6 15) (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 6 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING TRUE
-- C08  Art 1(2) is deleted in V2a (V2a src:6 is a placeholder): silent from 28 Sep 2021
#ASSERT REFUSED `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 2 1) (YMD 2022 2 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2021 9 27) (YMD 2021 9 1) (YMD 2021 9 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2021 9 10
#ASSERT REFUSED `on what day is a Law deemed to have been passed` (YMD 2021 9 28) (YMD 2021 9 1) (YMD 2021 9 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
-- C09  V1 src:6, src:10, src:9: a Law passed (confirmed and registered) on 2020-06-10, silent as to commencement: start of 2020-06-10
#ASSERT `day of commencement` (`stated as` `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation` NOTHING (YMD 2020 6 10)) `reading by commencement` EQUALS YMD 2020 6 10

§ `D. Article 1(3): passing and repeal read as making and rescission`

-- D01  V1 src:7: a reference to the passing of regulations, where appropriate, is a reference to their making
#ASSERT `how is a reference to passing or repeal read` (YMD 2020 6 1) `passing` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the making of the enactment`
-- D02  V1 src:7: a reference to the repeal of regulations is a reference to their rescission
#ASSERT `how is a reference to passing or repeal read` (YMD 2020 6 1) `repeal` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the rescission of the enactment`
